# Squash solo - Ladder: Side to Side
@description Side wall to side wall in fifteen levels, from single drives to continuous volleys,
  moving up and down the court on the way. Based on The Pursuit of Squash.
@speech rate 1.1
@minimum gap 0:00.8
@workout squash
@artwork ../images/squash.jpg
@include ../shared/squash.overtone

## Intro
Side to side ladder: side wall to side wall, from the middle of the court. Wear goggles. Play the
chapter for your level and repeat it until you reach the target, then move on to the next. After a
miss, count from zero.

// The Pursuit of Squash, Side to Side Challenges: side wall to side wall from the middle of the court.
## Level 1A: Forehand across
@ladder
Forehand across. Stand in the middle of the court. Step forward and drive your forehand into the
right side wall, so it crosses to the left wall, bounces, and comes back to you. Catch it, and go
again.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five, each one off the sweet spot with your head still.
+0:00.7 Watch the ball onto the strings.
+0:00.7 Head still after you hit.
+0:00.7 Step forward into every shot.

## Level 1B: Backhand across
@ladder
Backhand across. Middle of the court. Step forward and drive your backhand into the left side wall,
so it crosses to the right wall, bounces, and comes back to you. Catch it, and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five, each one off the sweet spot with your head still.
+0:00.7 Watch the ball onto the strings.
+0:00.7 Head still after you hit.
+0:00.7 Step forward into every shot.

## Level 2A: Forehand, then backhand
@ladder
Forehand, then backhand. Middle of the court. Forehand drive into the right wall, so it crosses to
the left wall and bounces, then drive it back with your backhand. Pick it up, and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five pairs without a break.
+0:00.7 Racket up before each shot.
+0:00.7 Watch the ball. Head still.

## Level 2B: Backhand, then forehand
@ladder
Backhand, then forehand. Middle of the court. Backhand drive into the left wall, so it crosses to
the right wall and bounces, then drive it back with your forehand. Pick it up, and go again.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five pairs without a break.
+0:00.7 Racket up before each shot.
+0:00.7 Watch the ball. Head still.

## Level 3: Continuous
@ladder
Continuous. Middle of the court. Drive into either side wall so it crosses to the other wall and
bounces, and keep it going, forehand, backhand. Let it peak just in front of you, as on a drive down
the wall. The further back you stand, the harder it gets.
+0:00.7 Target: fifty without a break.
+0:00.7 Hit it at the top of the bounce.
+0:00.7 Balanced. Head still.

## Level 4A: Moving forward
@ladder
Moving forward. Start behind the T, facing the front wall. Side to sides with a bounce, each one
angled slightly forward, so you work your way to the front wall. Touch it with your racket, then
work your way back past the T.
+0:00.7 Target: once, under control.
+0:00.7 Small steps. Stay balanced.
+0:00.7 Lost it? Back behind the T and start again.
+0:00.7 Watch the ball. Head still.

## Level 4B: Facing the back wall
@ladder
Facing the back wall. Start behind the T, facing the back wall. Angle each shot so it lands just
behind you, and walk backwards to the front wall. When you reach it, work your way forwards past the
T.
+0:00.7 Target: once, under control.
+0:00.7 Small steps. Stay balanced.
+0:00.7 Lost it? Back behind the T and start again.
+0:00.7 Watch the ball. Head still.

## Level 5A: Turn at the front wall
@ladder
Turn at the front wall. Behind the T, facing the front wall. Work forward with a bounce each time,
touch the front wall with your racket, turn round on the spot, and work back past the T facing the
back wall.
+0:00.7 Target: once, under control.
+0:00.7 Stay balanced through the turn.
+0:00.7 Lost it? Back behind the T and start again.
+0:00.7 Watch the ball. Head still.

## Level 5B: Backwards, then turn
@ladder
Backwards, then turn. Behind the T, facing the back wall. Walk backwards to the front wall with a
bounce each time, turn round on the spot, and work back past the T facing the front wall.
+0:00.7 Target: once, under control.
+0:00.7 Stay balanced through the turn.
+0:00.7 Lost it? Back behind the T and start again.
+0:00.7 Watch the ball. Head still.

## Level 6A: Two forehand volleys, one backhand
@ladder
Two forehand volleys, one backhand. Middle of the court. Two forehand volleys into the side wall,
then volley the next one on your backhand into the other wall, and catch it. That's one set.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five sets without a break.
+0:00.7 Short punch. Racket up.
+0:00.7 Clean hits. Don't carry the ball.

## Level 6B: Two backhand volleys, one forehand
@ladder
Two backhand volleys, one forehand. Middle of the court. Two backhand volleys into the side wall,
then volley the next one on your forehand into the other wall, and catch it. That's one set.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five sets without a break.
+0:00.7 Short punch. Racket up.
+0:00.7 Clean hits. Don't carry the ball.

## Level 7: Twenty-five each side
@ladder
Twenty-five each side. Middle of the court. Twenty-five forehand volleys into the side wall without
a break, pause, then twenty-five backhand volleys. A miss anywhere means starting again from the
first forehand.
+0:00.7 Target: both sets, back to back.
+0:00.7 Steady rhythm. Racket up.
+0:00.7 Missed? Back to the forehands.
+0:00.7 Firm wrist. Short punch.

## Level 8: Five a side
@ladder
Five a side. Middle of the court. Serve into the side wall and volley five on your forehand side,
counting the serve, then send the next one across and volley five on your backhand. Keep switching
without a bounce.
+0:00.7 Target: ten switches, fifty volleys.
+0:00.7 Count each side out loud.
+0:00.7 Racket up between every volley.

## Level 9: Two a side
@ladder
Two a side. Middle of the court. Volley twice on each side, then switch, without a bounce.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five switches, fifty volleys.
+0:00.7 Two, then across.
+0:00.7 Racket up between every volley.

## Level 10: Side to side volleys
@ladder
Side to side volleys. Middle of the court, balanced, feet level or one slightly ahead. Volley from
side wall to side wall without a bounce, and don't carry the ball.
+0:00.7 Target: twenty-five switches without a break.
+0:00.7 Balanced. Head still.
+0:00.7 Clean hits. Short punch.
